47
00:02:50,310 --> 00:02:54,270
Episode 16:
Acrobatic Football

48
00:02:50,310 --> 00:02:54,270
Translation: ARE-YOU-SURE
AreyousureSubs Presents

49
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:54,270
Me? To Toho Academy?

50
00:02:54,270 --> 00:02:57,090
As you know, Toho Academy is...

51
00:02:57,090 --> 00:03:00,780
...a famous school focused on developing professional footballers.

52
00:03:00,780 --> 00:03:04,370
We are almost ready to invite you.

53
00:03:04,370 --> 00:03:07,950
Hyuga-kun, of course we will look at your football skills...

54
00:03:07,950 --> 00:03:12,540
...as well as your character and daily lifestyle.

55
00:03:12,540 --> 00:03:15,560
If you join our academy...

56
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:20,130
...we will cover all your daily and academic expenses
throughout middle school, high school, and university—about 10 years.

57
00:03:20,130 --> 00:03:23,970
We'll cover all your daily and academic expenses
for about 10 years—through middle, high school, and university.

58
00:03:23,970 --> 00:03:25,220
Are you serious?!

59
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:26,840
We are.

60
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,430
If you join our academy...

61
00:03:28,430 --> 00:03:31,310
...you can focus on the football you love.

62
00:03:32,940 --> 00:03:35,480
But we have conditions.

63
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:36,760
Conditions?

64
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:37,900
Yes.

65
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:39,550
You're not the only one we're considering.

66
00:03:39,550 --> 00:03:42,120
We were thinking of one more forward...

67
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:45,200
...Ozora Tsubasa-kun.

68
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:49,890
We said let the winner of the previous match decide who it will be.

69
00:03:49,890 --> 00:03:52,580
Meiwa won that match.

70
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:58,270
But from that match, we found it a little hard to tell
whether Tsubasa-kun or you is better as a forward.

71
00:03:58,270 --> 00:04:00,690
...whether Tsubasa-kun or you is better as a forward.

72
00:04:00,690 --> 00:04:01,940
What are you saying?!

73
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:03,720
I'll never lose to him!

74
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:05,580
It's obvious that I'm better!

75
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:07,300
And we won the match!

76
00:04:07,300 --> 00:04:09,390
Prove it to us by winning the tournament.

77
00:04:09,390 --> 00:04:10,310
What?

78
00:04:10,310 --> 00:04:13,600
If you're the best as you say...

79
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:15,860
...prove it by winning the tournament.

80
00:04:15,860 --> 00:04:18,880
If you succeed, without a doubt...

81
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:22,280
...Toho Academy will offer you a football scholarship.

82
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:23,990
Are you serious?

83
00:04:23,990 --> 00:04:25,910
Yes. I don't lie.

84
00:04:25,910 --> 00:04:28,620
Alright! I'll definitely win and prove it!

85
00:04:35,270 --> 00:04:40,130
Even if you're second in the group stage, you advance to the qualifiers.

86
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:44,980
Keep in mind that there's a possibility you'll face Tsubasa-kun once again.

87
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:54,050
Meanwhile, Nankatsu, captained by Tsubasa...

88
00:04:54,050 --> 00:04:56,970
...put aside the shock of their defeat against Meiwa...

89
00:04:56,980 --> 00:05:01,640
...and crushed Fukuoka's Osu SS by an overwhelming 9-0...

90
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:04,690
...earning their first victory in the group.

91
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:02,950
Tsubasa-kun!

92
00:05:02,950 --> 00:05:04,690
We won! We won! We won!

93
00:05:04,690 --> 00:05:07,160
Alright! That makes it 1-1!

94
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:08,950
Let's keep this up...

95
00:05:08,950 --> 00:05:10,950
...and advance from the group!

96
00:05:10,950 --> 00:05:13,740
You're being so naive!

97
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:15,540
What did you say?

98
00:05:15,540 --> 00:05:17,430
The winners of Group 1...

99
00:05:17,430 --> 00:05:20,000
...will be Meiwa and us, Hanawa.

100
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,660
You mean Hanawa Youth Football Club from Akita?

101
00:05:23,660 --> 00:05:30,390
We played the Osu team you just beat this morning and won 10-0.

102
00:05:30,390 --> 00:05:32,510
They scored one more goal than us.

103
00:05:32,510 --> 00:05:34,430
Exactly.

104
00:05:34,430 --> 00:05:37,180
Wait, aren't these the kids from the train station?

105
00:05:38,310 --> 00:05:39,460
Masao!

106
00:05:39,460 --> 00:05:40,750
Nice pass!

107
00:05:40,750 --> 00:05:46,860
Yes. These two play in perfect sync and have amazing chemistry.

108
00:05:46,860 --> 00:05:50,820
Watch the match we're about to play carefully.

109
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:59,460
Hanawa Youth Football Club and Shimabara FC from Group 1.

110
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:01,540
It will start with Hanawa's kick-off.

111
00:06:02,670 --> 00:06:04,450
Alright! Let's go, Masao!

112
00:06:04,450 --> 00:06:05,420
Alright, Kazuo!

113
00:06:13,680 --> 00:06:15,220
We did it!

114
00:06:15,220 --> 00:06:16,470
Yes!

115
00:06:18,770 --> 00:06:21,650
Hanawa FC 7 - 0 Shimabara FC

116
00:06:23,190 --> 00:06:25,440
Hanawa played very dominantly.

117
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:26,870
They were great.

118
00:06:26,870 --> 00:06:30,070
I can't wait for our match against Hanawa.

119
00:06:30,070 --> 00:06:32,740
Yes, I can't wait either.

120
00:06:32,740 --> 00:06:33,450
Win.

121
00:06:33,450 --> 00:06:36,700
We will win. Brazil is waiting for me.

122
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:43,240
The next day, Nankatsu easily won their morning and afternoon matches...

123
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:47,210
...and reached 3 wins, 1 loss.

124
00:06:47,210 --> 00:06:48,520
That's it! We did it!

125
00:06:48,520 --> 00:06:49,470
That's 3!

126
00:06:49,470 --> 00:06:52,730
And now they began preparing for tomorrow's match against Hanawa...

127
00:06:52,730 --> 00:06:57,220
...which will determine who advances from the group stage.

128
00:06:57,220 --> 00:07:03,460
That afternoon, the two undefeated teams in Group 1...

129
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:05,900
...Meiwa and Hanawa faced each other, and...

130
00:07:08,070 --> 00:07:08,730
That's it!

131
00:07:08,730 --> 00:07:09,820
We did it!

132
00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:13,410
Meiwa FC 5 - 5 Hanawa FC

133
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,160
They drew with Meiwa?

134
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:15,370
Then if we draw instead of win tomorrow against Hanawa...

135
00:07:15,370 --> 00:07:18,370
...we won't be able to advance.

136
00:07:23,370 --> 00:07:27,420
Tomorrow we have a match against Hanawa Youth Football Club.

137
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:31,260
If we don't win this match, we can't advance.

138
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:36,200
So, to prepare for tomorrow, I'll explain Hanawa's strong points.

139
00:07:36,200 --> 00:07:40,100
Kids, remember Hanawa's match against Shimabara FC.

140
00:07:41,030 --> 00:07:46,730
The trait of this team is the amazing chemistry of their forwards, the Tachibana Brothers.

141
00:07:46,730 --> 00:07:53,650
When those two attack, the rest of the team stays in midfield and concentrates on defense.

142
00:07:53,700 --> 00:07:56,530
The flow of the game is decided by those two.

143
00:07:56,530 --> 00:07:59,080
Yes. Shimabara couldn't do anything.

144
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:03,490
If we disrupt Hanawa's great team chemistry...

145
00:08:03,490 --> 00:08:05,640
...we can secure Nankatsu's victory.

146
00:08:05,640 --> 00:08:07,210
I have a plan for that.

147
00:08:07,210 --> 00:08:08,040
Tsubasa.

148
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:08,880
Yes?

149
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:09,710
Misaki.

150
00:08:09,710 --> 00:08:10,590
Yes?

151
00:08:10,590 --> 00:08:13,220
I'll give you two a task.

152
00:08:18,860 --> 00:08:21,220
We have a big responsibility.

153
00:08:21,220 --> 00:08:22,300
Yes.

154
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:26,440
But I think it's a good way to disrupt their chemistry.

155
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:29,040
I'm counting on you for tomorrow, Misaki-kun.

156
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:32,540
Me too. We won't let Hanawa score even one goal--

157
00:08:35,180 --> 00:08:36,420
Are you scared?

158
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:38,660
You should join too!

159
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:42,080
Pillow fight!

160
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:42,910
Alright!

161
00:08:42,910 --> 00:08:44,290
Bring it on!

162
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:47,810
That hurt.

163
00:08:47,810 --> 00:08:50,420
Nishio-kun, I'm sorry.

164
00:08:50,420 --> 00:08:51,440
Goal!

165
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:53,260
You're a real forward, Tsubasa!

166
00:08:53,260 --> 00:08:56,260
Shut up! Take this!

167
00:08:57,240 --> 00:08:58,730
What's wrong, Nishio?

168
00:08:58,730 --> 00:09:00,430
I'm an iron goalkeeper!

169
00:09:00,430 --> 00:09:03,270
Why don't you say that in front of Wakabayashi-san?

170
00:09:03,270 --> 00:09:05,430
Take my shot!

171
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:08,230
Alright!

172
00:09:08,230 --> 00:09:09,020
Take it!

173
00:09:09,020 --> 00:09:10,690
Nice shot!

174
00:09:10,690 --> 00:09:17,560
- Take that!
- Go!

175
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:20,570
Kids, let's defeat Hanawa with this strength!

176
00:09:20,570 --> 00:09:22,240
Yes!

177
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:30,770
At the end of the second day of the tournament...

178
00:09:30,770 --> 00:09:33,870
...we've seen all the promising players, haven't we?

179
00:09:33,870 --> 00:09:39,110
Except for Nankatsu SC's goalkeeper, Wakabayashi Genzo, who didn't participate.

180
00:09:39,110 --> 00:09:40,220
Yes.

181
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:42,690
Despite being 5th grade, he captained Shutetsu Elementary...

182
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:46,740
...and became champion last year without conceding a single goal—a prodigy.

183
00:09:46,740 --> 00:09:49,310
There's no one like him in his generation.

184
00:09:49,310 --> 00:09:52,200
What about Nakanishi Taichi from Naniwa FC?

185
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:53,660
He's also a good goalkeeper.

186
00:09:53,660 --> 00:09:56,710
Unexpectedly agile for his large build.

187
00:09:56,710 --> 00:10:00,470
Even though he's that big, it's a shame he can't rival Wakabayashi.

188
00:10:00,470 --> 00:10:02,370
What do you think about the midfielders?

189
00:10:02,370 --> 00:10:06,390
The ones who left a good impression are Misaki Taro from Nankatsu...

190
00:10:06,390 --> 00:10:11,460
...Matsuyama Hikaru from Furano, and Sawada Takeshi from Meiwa FC.

191
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:14,810
I'll consider Takeshi-kun in 2 years since he's in 4th grade, but...

192
00:10:14,810 --> 00:10:17,880
...Misaki-kun and Matsuyama-kun are the players I want.

193
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:19,880
Matsuyama Hikaru...

194
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:21,990
Isn't he a bit lacking technically?

195
00:10:22,510 --> 00:10:30,750
He carried the elementary school team he captained to the national tournament thanks to potential and determination rather than technique.

196
00:10:30,750 --> 00:10:34,250
After he joins, we can work on his technique.

197
00:10:35,170 --> 00:10:41,450
But regarding midfielders, Misugi Jun from Musashi FC really stands out more.

198
00:10:41,450 --> 00:10:46,300
Besides being a great playmaker, he's also a very talented goal scorer.

199
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:52,710
Coach Kitazume from middle school also mentioned that he wants us to develop his goal-scoring abilities.

200
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:55,730
Without a doubt, the forwards we most want...

201
00:10:55,730 --> 00:11:00,880
...are Ozora Tsubasa from Nankatsu SC and Hyuga Kojiro from Meiwa FC.

202
00:11:00,880 --> 00:11:04,340
Even though we've had our eyes on Tsubasa-kun since the regional tournament...

203
00:11:04,340 --> 00:11:07,860
...he has really shined at the national tournament since yesterday.

204
00:11:07,860 --> 00:11:11,800
If he couldn't do this much, he wouldn't be suitable for our academy anyway.

205
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:16,790
I want to see those two face off once again.

206
00:11:16,790 --> 00:11:19,780
Me too. In the finals.

207
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:25,320
The third day of the tournament and the last matches of the group stage.

208
00:11:25,910 --> 00:11:32,960
Furano, putting everything into the game, won all 5 matches.

209
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:38,010
Musashi FC also advanced from the group stage with 5 wins...

210
00:11:38,010 --> 00:11:41,220
...while Captain Misugi rested on the bench.

211
00:11:41,220 --> 00:11:45,880
Meiwa showed their overwhelming power in their final matches and...

212
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:47,970
...finished with 4 wins, 1 draw.

213
00:11:47,970 --> 00:11:53,770
Nankatsu's opponents in the qualifiers were set.

214
00:11:53,770 --> 00:11:59,400
In the final match of the group stage, the team advancing to the qualifiers will be determined.

215
00:11:59,410 --> 00:12:02,860
The Nankatsu-Hanawa match is about to begin.

216
00:12:02,860 --> 00:12:11,320
In their historic match against Meiwa, Nankatsu let victory slip away at the last moment.

217
00:12:11,450 --> 00:12:15,750
On the other hand, Hanawa had drawn.

218
00:12:15,750 --> 00:12:19,380
The stadium is packed with enthusiastic spectators eager to watch the match.

219
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:20,980
Listen up, kids.

220
00:12:20,980 --> 00:12:24,880
Today's match is crucial because it will determine the team going to the qualifiers.

221
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:27,710
Win no matter what and advance!

222
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:28,600
Okay!

223
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:32,060
Good, stick to the plan, Tsubasa and Misaki.

224
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:33,140
Okay!

225
00:12:35,140 --> 00:12:37,960
Both teams have taken the field.

226
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:40,110
I'm counting on you, everyone.

227
00:12:40,110 --> 00:12:43,690
Akita representative Hanawa has 3 wins and 1 draw so far.

228
00:12:43,690 --> 00:12:46,810
With the Tachibana Brothers as forwards, the remaining team concentrates on defense.

229
00:12:46,810 --> 00:12:50,150
A very unique team.

230
00:12:50,150 --> 00:12:54,200
On the other hand, Shizuoka representative Nankatsu has 3 wins and 1 loss.

231
00:12:54,200 --> 00:13:00,210
They display great team play with ace forward Tsubasa-kun at the center.

232
00:13:00,210 --> 00:13:05,260
Fans of both teams have started cheering even before the match begins!

233
00:13:05,260 --> 00:13:10,000
Amidst loud cheers, the match is about to start with Hanawa's kick-off!

234
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:15,810
Will Nankatsu or Hanawa advance to the qualifiers?

235
00:13:15,810 --> 00:13:17,760
Alright, let's score a goal today too!

236
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:18,150
Okay!

237
00:13:18,150 --> 00:13:21,900
As usual, Hanawa tries to find an opening with the Tachibana Brothers' attack.

238
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:26,150
Everyone, only they are attacking! Stop them no matter what!

239
00:13:26,150 --> 00:13:27,120
Let's go!

240
00:13:27,120 --> 00:13:30,660
Can Nankatsu stop them?

241
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:38,330
What?

242
00:13:38,760 --> 00:13:39,730
It's no use!

243
00:13:39,730 --> 00:13:43,840
Even the famous Nankatsu can't intervene as this duo cuts through the midfield!

244
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:46,840
Why? Why did they pass us so easily?

245
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:50,850
Tachibana Masao-kun and Kazuo-kun are showing wonderful chemistry today.

246
00:13:50,850 --> 00:13:53,430
Are they going to score a goal right after the match starts?

247
00:13:53,430 --> 00:13:54,640
I won't allow it!

248
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:55,460
Hey!

249
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:56,520
Nice pass!

250
00:13:59,020 --> 00:14:00,810
We will be your opponents!

251
00:14:00,810 --> 00:14:02,200
What?!

252
00:14:04,990 --> 00:14:09,990
Translation: ARE-YOU-SURE
AreyousureSubs Presents

253
00:14:10,030 --> 00:14:13,070
What's this? Tsubasa-kun, normally a center forward...

254
00:14:13,070 --> 00:14:14,450
...has come back this far.

